  "_exec_summary": [
    {
      "ESSeqNum": 0,
      "FacilityID": 1000120822,
      "SummaryText": "**Please Note: Blank/Empty Boxes are intended to be Blank. Esubmit portal doesn't allow to fill in sections with No or N/A.  \n\nExecutive Summary:\n \nSwan Ranch Railroad is a short line railroad owned and operated by Watco Companies, LLC.  Tank cars (railcars) containing regulated and non-regulated chemicals are received, staged for temporary storage, and released for further distribution.  \n\nEPA\u0092s Risk Management Plan (RMP) Rule applies because more than threshold quantities of Propane (CAS No. 74-98-6) and Butane (CAS No.  106-97-8) can be present on-site at any one time.  Specific regulated processes are:\n\u0095\tRailcars containing Propane, with a total on-site storage of greater than 10,000 pounds; and\n\u0095\tRailcars containing Butane, with a total on-site storage of greater than 10,000 pounds.\n\nBased on the criteria spelled out at 40 CFR 68.10, the Swan Ranch Cheyenne Rail, LLC falls under Program 2 eligibility requirements due to the following:\na)\tThe above-referenced regulated processes are not eligible for Program level 1 (because public receptors would be impacted in a worst-case scenario); and \nb)\tThe above-referenced regulated processes are not subject to Program level 3 requirements.\n\nRMP Rule implementation practices for each of the applicable Chemical Accident Prevention Provisions found under 40 CFR Part 68 and Program 2 Prevention Program elements found at 40 CFR 68.48 thru 68.62 are prescribed under a written RMP Program Manual.  Compliance audits are performed at least once every 3 years to assess Swan Ranch Railroad's conformance with their written RMP Program Manual and applicable RMP Rule regulations.\n\nNo loading or unloading of the railcars occurs while on-site.  In fact, railcars are not opened while onsite for any reason.  Maintenance, including hot work, is not typically performed on railcars while on-site.  If such is required (emergency situations only), such would be performed by a third-party contractor competent in the scope of work required.\n\nSw"
    },
    {
      "ESSeqNum": 1,
      "FacilityID": 1000120822,
      "SummaryText": "an Ranch Railroad is a non-responding facility.  Therefore, in the unlikely event of an emergency relating to one or more tank car containing Propane and/or Butane, site personnel would react defensively and utilize the services of local emergency response providers for active remediation.  This response strategy is prescribed under the site's Emergency Response Program, communicated to site personnel via training and awareness programs, and coordinated with local emergency response providers."
    }
  ]
